  "knownLimitations": [
    "The generated Vercel deployment URLs are protected; passing their bypass-backed smoke checks does not prove anonymous public access.",
    "Vercel automatically classified the first project deployment as production during project bootstrap even though --prod was not requested. The first staged candidate is also retained as superseded history because it compiled the owner's corrected-away .com canonical origin; neither historical deployment is the intended Phase 6A candidate.",
    "The historical Phase 6A public funding-intent screenshot gap remains: both existing public invoices are terminal, and producing that evidence would have required creating and broadcasting a new on-chain invoice. Phase 6B2 deterministic funding fixtures stop before the final wallet action and are not represented as live public evidence.",
    "The 1,000-record production-log review is a bounded sample beginning at 2026-08-12T15:30:23Z, not a complete traffic count.",
    "The 17 Phase 6B2 captures and automated accessibility checks do not prove human usability or WCAG conformance.",
    "The protected Phase 4B invoice-1 verifier compares current party balances with a historical snapshot that became stale after invoice 2 changed the same wallets. Current invoice-1 evidence therefore uses five receipt-reconciliation checks rather than claiming that legacy script passes end to end.",
    "The corrected pre-mutation evidence establishes that the ProofPay host did not exist. Unrelated DNS preservation is supported by the single scoped Cloudflare create action rather than a complete pre-change export of the full zone.",
    "ProofPay uses Coston2 test assets and is not audited, mainnet-ready, legal escrow, fiat escrow, or production-security evidence. Receipt commitments prove byte integrity, not delivery truth or quality."
  ]
